    <body>
        <segment id="1" parent="13" relname="span">I think intuitiveness in software should be measured based on the intended audience or end-users of the product.</segment>
        <segment id="2" parent="3" relname="concession">For instance UML design tool may be very intuitive to the average systems analyst</segment>
        <segment id="3" parent="14" relname="span">but it may prove to be quite difficult to learn and use, wihtout help, for the average user who spends most of their time typing documents and surfing the web.</segment>
        <segment id="4" parent="15" relname="span">The intuitiveness of a user interface can be greatly increased or decreased based on how the interface is designed.</segment>
        <segment id="5" parent="19" relname="span">In an article entitled E-Tail vs. Retail Larry Marine discussed some of the problems that E-Tail sites face that could potentially lead to failures.</segment>
        <segment id="6" parent="20" relname="span">he argued that E-Tail sites must capture the essence of traditional stores</segment>
        <segment id="7" parent="6" relname="volitional-result">if these sites should be successful.</segment>
        <segment id="8" parent="19" relname="elaboration">He went on to say that E-Tail sites should provide consumers with a place to enjoy impressive service, and ease of purchasing products.</segment>
        <segment id="9" parent="10" relname="nonvolitional-cause">We'vee all seen those sites that are cluttered with flash movies an so forth that distracts the consumer.</segment>
        <segment id="10" parent="21" relname="span">These distractions can take away from a site being intuitive.</segment>
        <segment id="11" parent="17" relname="summary">To achieve intuitiveness in UI designers should make use of objects that end-users can relate to.</segment>
        <group id="12" type="multinuc"/>
        <group id="13" type="span" parent="12" relname="joint"/>
        <group id="14" type="span" parent="1" relname="elaboration"/>
        <group id="15" type="span" parent="12" relname="joint"/>
        <group id="16" type="span" parent="4" relname="elaboration"/>
        <group id="17" type="span" parent="16" relname="span"/>
        <group id="18" type="span" parent="17" relname="span"/>
        <group id="19" type="span" parent="18" relname="span"/>
        <group id="20" type="span" parent="5" relname="elaboration"/>
        <group id="21" type="span" parent="18" relname="elaboration"/>
    </body>
